Fixed-pitch propeller with blade-element / momentum aerodynamics and
dynamic (uniform) inflow, mounted at body point r_hub with thrust along -z_body.

Blade element (linear twist, uniform inflow), dimensional form so that a
stopped rotor is well defined:
  T = rho*A*(sigma*a/2) * [theta75/3*(OR)^2 + cf*Vxy_eff^2 - (Vc + vi)*OR/2],
  cf = (theta75 - theta_tw/4)/2,  OR = Omega*R,
  Vxy_eff^2 = Vxy^2 * OR^2 / (OR^2 + Vxy^2/mu_max^2)  (caps advance ratio at mu_max)
Dynamic inflow (Pitt-Peters apparent mass m_a = 8/3*rho*R^3):
  m_a * dvi/dt = T - 2*rho*A*vi*sqrt(Vxy^2 + (Vc + vi)^2)
Shaft torque = induced/climb power + profile power:
  Q = (Vc + vi)*T/Omega + rho*A*R*sigma*Cd0/8 * OR*|OR|*(1 + 4.65*mu_eff^2)
Rotor drag (H-force): F_H = -k_H * Omega * (in-plane air-relative velocity).

theta75 and Cd0 are calibrated so that static thrust and power equal the
propeller-convention coefficients CT0 (T = CT0*rho*n^2*D^4) and CP0
(P = CP0*rho*n^3*D^5).

Rotor spin: angular velocity = spin * Omega * z_body (spin = +1 clockwise seen
from above, -1 counter-clockwise). The rotor inertia J carries the spin
momentum; its gyroscopic moment and the motor housing reaction (support) are
transferred to the airframe through `mount`.

